Package: ryzen-smu-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: ryzenadj (>= 0.17.0)
Description: ryzen_smu kernel module for AMD Ryzen SMU access (DKMS)
 The ryzen_smu kernel module exposes the System Management Unit of AMD Ryzen
 processors through sysfs. RyzenAdj uses it in preference to /dev/mem when a
 compatible version is loaded.
 .
 This matters with Secure Boot on: Secure Boot puts the kernel in lockdown,
 which blocks the /dev/mem access RyzenAdj otherwise needs, but still loads a
 module signed with an enrolled key. DKMS builds the module for every installed
 kernel and signs it. On Ubuntu it uses the machine owner key from
 shim-signed and asks once, on the next boot, to enroll it; on Debian the key
 DKMS generates has to be enrolled with mokutil.
 .
 The module is loaded at boot through modules-load.d.
